# Domain Purity

The domain layer is the canonical, engine-agnostic core. It is imported by Blender/UPBGE,
Godot exporters and the backend, so it must depend on nothing but the stdlib and itself.

- Never import `bpy`, `mathutils`, `godot`, `fastapi`, `sqlalchemy`, or `backend.*`.
- No file/network I/O in the domain: loading JSON belongs to `character_engine.loader`,
  writing artifacts belongs to `character_engine.export` or `infrastructure/`.
- Prefer frozen `@dataclass` value objects and explicit exceptions from
  `character_engine.domain.anatomy.osteology.exceptions` / `character_engine.exceptions`.
- Coordinates are `tuple[float, float, float]` in the canonical frame (Z-up, -Y forward, metres).

```python
# ❌ BAD — engine leak into the domain
import bpy
def build(skeleton): bpy.data.armatures.new(skeleton.name)

# ✅ GOOD — domain produces data; infrastructure/blender consumes it
def build(skeleton) -> list[BoneSpec]: ...
```

`python scripts/lint.py` fails the build if `bpy` is imported outside
`src/character_engine/infrastructure/` or `runtime/`.
